{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:16c195feecc1ee46","name":"Dark Jedi Master","source":{"id":"source:reference-16c195feecc1ee46","title":"Dark Jedi Master","revision":18890,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T20:55:37Z","sha256":"642e60962c63ff6b85b6d0a6257f6b7290842165d9ce1fef8884801431a1daea","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=18890","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Dark%20Jedi%20Master&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-16c195feecc1ee46","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Threats of the Galaxy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Threats_of_the_Galaxy"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The Dark Jedi are Force-attuned individuals who reject the teachings of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Jedi"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Jedi","referenceId":"reference:d320edb17de6c558"}," and, for some, ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Sith"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Sith","referenceId":"reference:32bde5e69837ac8e"},". Most are fallen Jedi who have failed to live up to the ideals and lifestyle of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Jedi"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Jedi","referenceId":"reference:d320edb17de6c558"}," and instead embrace the baser emotions that lead to corruption and evil. Every Dark Jedi is a tragedy, a terrible shame that stains the illustrious history of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Jedi Order"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Jedi_Order"},", but when a Jedi Master falls, it is a tragedy beyond compare.\n"]},"\n\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Dark Jedi Master Encounters"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Dark Jedi Masters are excellent high-level villains for just about any era. Since Dark Jedi are not bound by the Rule of Two that limits the number of Sith in the galaxy, Dark Jedi Masters can coexist with the Emperor and any of his apprentices (",{"tag":"a","children":["Darth Maul"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Darth_Maul","referenceId":"reference:087d6f5867f2441a"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Darth Tyranus"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Darth_Tyranus"},", or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Darth Vader"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Darth_Vader","referenceId":"reference:c167be702b56cffc"},"). Dark Jedi Masters have their own Dark Jedi apprentices, and there's no limit to the number of cronies they might employ.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Although many Dark Jedi Masters have grand designs of their own, hatching evil plots in the shadows of the galaxy, some, such as ",{"tag":"a","children":["Jerec"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jerec","referenceId":"reference:0b5fc69ea7e3d9a3"},", are actually in the employ of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Sith"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Sith","referenceId":"reference:32bde5e69837ac8e"},", serving as Imperial Inquisitors, Hands of the Emperor, or in just about any other capacity the Dark lord of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Sith"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Sith","referenceId":"reference:32bde5e69837ac8e"}," can conceive.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Dark Jedi Master Statistics (CL 17)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Medium ",{"tag":"a","children":["Jedi"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jedi","referenceId":"reference:0b0e48747027a29d"}," 9/",{"tag":"a","children":["Jedi Knight"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jedi_Knight","referenceId":"reference:8a1e23d924066b37"}," 5/",{"tag":"a","children":["Jedi Master"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jedi_Master","referenceId":"reference:5fac760c8a2485ba"}," 3\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Destiny Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Destiny_Points"},":"]}," 1; ",{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Force Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Points"},":"]}," 6, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Strong in the Force"],"hr